# orbit-safe: what opens the safe. It runs as the session's own user, so
# pam_unix checks that user's password through unix_chkpwd.
#
# More factors go above or below the password, and the safe shows each
# module's question as it asks:
#   a fingerprint first:   auth sufficient pam_fprintd.so
#   the face (howdy):      auth sufficient pam_howdy.so
#   a code from the phone, after the password (libpam-google-authenticator,
#   set up with google-authenticator):
#                          auth required pam_google_authenticator.so
@include common-auth
@include common-account
